# platform.linux.sdl

mm.display and mm.touch over SDL2, in one module and bound twice. SDL has one
video subsystem, one window, one event queue, and shared state between drawing
and input; two modules could not own that between them.

It exists for one thing the DRM provider cannot do: run in a window beside the
editor. DRM needs DRM master and a compositor holds it, so anything visual there
means leaving the session for a virtual terminal.

It names a library and is still not a lib. wrapper. Its public dependency is the
project interface module, not a foreign library API, which is the same ground on
which docs/modules-c++20.mdy already exempts a provider over a bridge ABI.

The window is the display provider's. Touch reports the pointer while the left
button is held, and answers Unsupported when no window exists, rather than
opening a second one.
